  "question": {
    "text": "Air is filled in a bottle at atmospheric pressure and it is corked at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mn>C</mn></math>. If the cork can come out at a pressure&nbsp;<math><mn>3&nbsp;</mn></math>times the atmospheric pressure, then up to what temperature should the bottle be heated in order to remove the cork.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
